@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "About Us";
}

<style>
    section {
        max-width: 800px;
        margin: 0 auto;
        text-align: center;
    }

    h1 {
        font-size: 3.5em;
        font-family: 'Roboto Slab', serif;
        text-align: left;
        margin-bottom: 20px;
    }

    h2, h3 {
        text-align: left;
        margin-top: 50px;
    }

    p {
        text-align: left;
        margin-bottom: 10px;
        max-width: 600px;
        margin-inline-start: 0;
        margin-inline-end: auto;
    }

        p:last-child {
            margin-bottom: 270px;
        }
</style>

<h1>@ViewData["Title"]</h1>

<section>
    <h2>Welcome to our Booking Management Website!</h2>

    <p>Here's a brief guide on how to navigate through our services:</p>

    <h3>Services Section</h3>
    <p>
        Our website is designed with two main sections: Services and Bookings.
        In the Services section, users can access three primary categories: Hotels, Flights, and Car Rentals.
        Within each category, users have the option to create new listings or browse existing ones.
    </p>

    <p>
        Creating a service allows users to add and modify details such as pricing, availability dates, and capacity.
        In the browse section, users can view all available services and perform actions like editing or deleting them (if no bookings have been made).
    </p>

    <h3>Bookings Section</h3>
    <p>
        Moving on to our Bookings section, users can make reservations for their desired services.
        After selecting a service, users are prompted to apply filters or preferences to refine their search.
        Once a suitable option is found, users provide additional booking details and confirm their reservation.
        Upon confirmation, a unique booking ID is generated and displayed for reference.
    </p>

    <p>
        To manage existing bookings, users can navigate to the browse section, select the relevant service, and input their booking ID.
        From there, they can view their booking details and choose to delete the booking if desired.
    </p>

    <h3>Database and Controllers</h3>
    <p>
        Our database is equipped with tables to store essential data, including Cars, Hotels, Flights, Bookings, and respective booking tables for each service type.
        For efficient management, we've implemented controllers for each service type, allowing for seamless CRUD operations on services and bookings.
    </p>

    <h3>Upcoming Features</h3>
    <p>
        Upcoming features include user sign-in functionality, enabling users to access and manage their past and upcoming bookings.
        We also plan to enhance search capabilities with additional filters and introduce more service attributes for a richer user experience.
    </p>

    <p>
        In the future, users will have the ability to consolidate different types of bookings under one reservation, enabling easy management and customization.
        Additionally, we'll introduce editing options for bookings, allowing users to modify select details for added flexibility.
    </p>

    <p>
        We're committed to continuously improving our platform to provide users with a seamless and comprehensive booking experience.
    </p>
</section>
